# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 4 ("the order of a group's lines decides positions and nothing else"), ch. 8 (a clause is chosen by its pattern) and ruling TC (places counted as built): loud gives `@Seven`'s 7, doubled by the local function to 14, so the widget's clause `k` builds "one 14" and "two 14" at 0 and 1 and `@Seven` its label at 2; soft gives 20, doubled to 40, and builds nothing in its arm. Never run: prismc refuses the program.
test loud

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Label(text="one 14")
    1: Ui.Label(text="two 14")
    2: Ui.Label(text="seven")

test soft

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Label(text="one 40")
    1: Ui.Label(text="two 40")
